--- (2) THE SENSITIVITY: WHICH BASELINE IS FAIR, AND THE DEVIATIONS ---
    THE FAIR COMPARISON for a real catalog: the SHMR-matched NFW ratio (G121's
    conventions) multiplied onto the LCDM-OBSERVED consensus (GAMA/MaNGA/zCOSMOS
    verified rows) for the absolute normalization.  The BARYON-ONLY baseline is the
    MECHANISM reference (G118's q = 1 curve -- the deep-regime force-ratio transfer),
    NOT a realizable control: a real catalog's selection lives in a universe with dark
    halos and its control (identical-cut LCDM mocks) already contains them.  The three
    baselines answer three different questions; only the SHMR-NFW x consensus pair
    produces a number a real catalog can confront.
    the observed consensus curve: f_obs(s) = 2.0% (s/30 kpc)^1.39 ((1+z)/1.1)^1.53;
    scale index beta = 1.393 derived from the committed GAMA counts (1434/4741/13496 at 20/50/100 kpc [V]); anchor band [1.5, 3.0]% at 30 kpc (zCOSMOS 1.6% [V], consensus 2.0% [V], MaNGA 3.0% [V]); the task anchor 5-10% [U -- not itself verified].
    cross-checks: f_obs(30, z=0.1) = 2.00% (the 2% consensus [V] EXACT); zCOSMOS at z=0.1: 1.63% [V]; MaNGA ~3% (1-30 kpc, z~0.04) [V]
